From 76c3741986e2432cc855c17a6d5354b4387b9b24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 22:22:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: smb347: take the USB input mode from CMD_B
 when setting the limit

Register CFG_PIN bit 4 (CFG_PIN_EN_CTRL) also hands the choice of the
USB5/1/HC input mode to the USB5/1/HC pins, and then CMD_B is ignored.
The Nexus 7 vendor driver clears it ("i2c register control") before it
selects high-current mode.

On the Samsung Galaxy Tab 2 10.1 the bootloader leaves it clear, but the
charger sets it again whenever it reloads its configuration, which it
does when its input power drops out (CFG_PIN reads 0x78 at that moment,
0x1c once the driver has programmed it again). After a USB replug,
writing input_current_limit then left the charger at 500 mA (STAT_E in
USB5 mode with CMD_B in high-current mode).

Clear the bit when selecting the mode through CMD_B, unless charging is
pin controlled, which needs the bit set.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/power/supply/smb347-charger.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/smb347-charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/smb347-charger.c
index d1b2ddeea27d..08b1e8b242d5 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/smb347-charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/smb347-charger.c
@@ -560,6 +560,21 @@ static int smb347_set_usb_input_limit(struct smb347_charger *smb,
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * CFG_PIN_EN_CTRL also makes the USB5/1/HC pins select the mode, and
+	 * then CMD_B is ignored. It is set at power-on reset, and by us for
+	 * pin control of charging; take the mode from CMD_B otherwise.
+	 */
+	switch (smb->enable_control) {
+	case SMB3XX_CHG_ENABLE_PIN_ACTIVE_LOW:
+	case SMB3XX_CHG_ENABLE_PIN_ACTIVE_HIGH:
+		break;
+	default:
+		ret = regmap_clear_bits(smb->regmap, CFG_PIN, CFG_PIN_EN_CTRL);
+		if (ret < 0)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
 	return regmap_update_bits(smb->regmap, CMD_B,
 				  CMD_B_HC_MODE | CMD_B_USB5, cmd_b);
 }
